Copy the project you are in into a new workspace

Usage: forkspace new [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]  Name for the new workspace (defaults to <project>-1, <project>-2, ...)

Options:
      --tmpfs          Keep the workspace's changes in RAM (Linux overlay only; lost on reboot)
      --no-fsync       Do not flush the workspace's writes on fsync (Linux overlay only; faster installs and builds, recent writes lost on power loss)
      --copy           Consent to a full directory copy backend
      --live           Show later changes to the source in the workspace (Linux overlay only; skips the frozen copy)
      --memory <SIZE>  Throttle the workspace's processes above this much memory, e.g. 4G (Linux)
      --cpu <PERCENT>  Cap the workspace's CPU time, as a percentage of one CPU, e.g. 200% (Linux)
  -h, --help           Print help
